"""memento: the route from Y's approval to a running system. No AI.

Y, 2026-11-28 04:00 (t117): "Claude asked for a clear route from merge
approval to deployment. Claude may create a helper program that sits on
his shoulder like a Roman returning, crossing the pomerium in triumph."
In a triumph a slave rode behind the general, holding the laurel over him
and whispering "respice post te, hominem te esse memento": look behind
you, remember you are mortal. This is that voice: it carries the
triumph, and checks every step of it.

    memento            the plan: the queued PRs, checked (open, reviewed,
                       mergeable) and put in a safe order. Changes nothing.
    memento propose comms-deck#173 chronophage#5 ...
                       queue PRs (any seat may propose; only Y merges)
    memento clear      empty the queue
    memento go         the plan, then (after Y types "yes" at a real
                       terminal) merge in that order, pull the live trees,
                       re-register hooks, make netwatch permanent, check
                       everything is healthy.
    memento --self-test

Authority stays with Y. A chat note can be sent as anyone by any agent, so
it can't be the trigger. `go` needs Y's "yes" typed at a terminal
